%-----------------------------------------------------------------------------!
% TITLE PAGE
% ----------
% Demeyere's three-zone architecture: teal letterspaced small-caps
% identity line over plain roman faculty/school/group; bold ~2x title at
% the optical centre; author and degree descending in weight. No rules,
% no crest, no ornament. Guidance 9.5 content order preserved.
%-----------------------------------------------------------------------------!
%=============================================================================!
% TITLE PAGE A - after Bacanu (Chemistry 2021, eprint 455367 p3), the
% cleanest instance of the Southampton "uosthesis" Palatino layout.
%
% The mechanism, not just the look: two FIXED anchor blocks with a
% FLOATING middle. Masthead baselines pinned at y/H 0.2006 / 0.2349 /
% 0.2549, colophon at 0.7697 / 0.7898 / 0.8581, and the title+author
% group optically box-centred in the 433.4 pt band between them by the
% template's own rule (three equal glues; the +3.70 / -9.60 pt offsets
% below are the ascender artefacts measured across Bacanu, Ashton,
% Bramley and Chowdhury). Five sizes, the 12 pt LaTeX ladder:
% 20.66 / 17.22 / 14.35 / 11.96 / 10.91. Bold on exactly two items,
% italic on the connective words, one accent colour.
%
% Deviations forced by Brad's content and by the rules: the identity
% line is set in REAL Palatino small caps at medium weight (the family
% has no bold small caps; Bacanu's is a faked bold small cap), and the
% axis is the text-block centre of a single-sided electronic volume,
% which here coincides with the paper centre - Bacanu's +18 pt recto
% offset is meaningless without a binding edge.
%=============================================================================!
\renewcommand\maketitle{%
   \btypeout{Title Page}
   \clearpage
   \newgeometry{top=25mm,bottom=25mm,left=31.75mm,right=31.75mm,
                headheight=0pt,headsep=0pt,footskip=0pt}%
   \thispagestyle{empty}%
   \begingroup
   \singlespacing
   \setlength{\parskip}{0pt}\setlength{\parindent}{0pt}%
   % \tpline{<baseline advance>}{<line>}: places one line, centred on the
   % measure, whose baseline sits exactly the given distance below the
   % previous baseline. \smash makes each line zero-height so the page is
